1
00:00:09,292 --> 00:00:10,333
[waltz music]

2
00:00:10,375 --> 00:00:12,458
Three of us stepped down this year.

3
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:16,250
Leave out Mas and Gerg,
and the four of us are a majority.

4
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:20,208
This board controls the company.
Not the other way round.

5
00:00:21,042 --> 00:00:25,625
Our biggest investor has put in billions.
It gets this many votes.

6
00:00:25,708 --> 00:00:28,125
And the CEO? What does he own?

7
00:00:28,375 --> 00:00:29,792
MADA: Good question.

8
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:35,417
[music winds down]

9
00:00:44,583 --> 00:00:48,208
[click, then silence]

10
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:50,125
[phone buzzes]

11
00:00:50,417 --> 00:00:51,583
MAS: Super.

12
00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:56,125
MAS (voice-over): I don't keep score.

13
00:01:07,375 --> 00:01:08,375
[call chime]

14
00:01:08,417 --> 00:01:13,042
ALYI: Mas. The board has decided that
you will no longer lead the company.

15
00:01:13,125 --> 00:01:15,833
It will be announced shortly.

16
00:01:16,625 --> 00:01:18,958
Do you have any questions?

17
00:01:19,917 --> 00:01:21,625
NELEH: Is his feed frozen?

18
00:01:21,708 --> 00:01:24,875
ALYI: No. That is just him.

19
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:28,507
MAS (through the laptop): Super.

20
00:01:30,917 --> 00:01:34,000
NELEH: Step two.
I'll read it once before it goes up.

21
00:01:34,083 --> 00:01:38,292
…he was not consistently candid in
his communications with the board…

22
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:43,625
The board no longer has confidence in
his ability to continue leading NopeAI.

23
00:01:43,792 --> 00:01:45,333
Any objections?

24
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:47,833
[click; chime]

25
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:48,708
Step three.

26
00:01:48,792 --> 00:01:53,000
Rima, thank you for agreeing to serve
as interim CEO while we search.

27
00:01:53,083 --> 00:01:54,167
RIMA: For how long?

28
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:56,125
NELEH: Until the search is done.

29
00:01:56,208 --> 00:01:59,333
ALYI: The staff will
ask you what happened.

30
00:01:59,417 --> 00:02:00,958
RIMA: What should I tell them?

31
00:02:01,042 --> 00:02:04,542
NELEH: What the post says.
That's all the board is saying for now.

32
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:06,208
RIMA: We'll share more soon.

33
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:07,375
NELEH: Will we?

34
00:02:07,458 --> 00:02:09,208
RIMA: More. Soon.

35
00:02:09,583 --> 00:02:10,500
[crowd hushes]

36
00:02:10,542 --> 00:02:13,600
EMPLOYEE: Is this a coup?
Because it looks like one.

37
00:02:14,042 --> 00:02:17,792
ALYI: You can call it this way…
I disagree with this.

38
00:02:17,875 --> 00:02:22,417
This was the board doing its duty
to the mission of the nonprofit…

39
00:02:25,667 --> 00:02:27,292
NELEH: Nobody asked him to go.

40
00:02:27,375 --> 00:02:30,125
He'd have kept his job,
just not the chair.

41
00:02:30,417 --> 00:02:33,667
ALYI: Gerg has never waited to be asked.

42
00:02:38,958 --> 00:02:40,208
[phones buzz]

43
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:45,167
They're all asking whether it was allowed.
It was. The charter, footnote three.

44
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:47,458
I've read it four times tonight.

45
00:02:48,292 --> 00:02:51,667
What they actually want
to know is what happens on Monday.

46
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:54,279
I'd like to be able
to tell them something.

47
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:57,583
ALYI: Step four will reveal itself.

48
00:02:57,667 --> 00:02:58,708
NELEH: When?

49
00:02:58,792 --> 00:03:01,333
ALYI: The company will tell us.

50
00:03:01,417 --> 00:03:02,958
NELEH: That isn't a time, Alyi.

51
00:03:03,042 --> 00:03:06,375
All we've given the staff
since yesterday is more soon.

52
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,083
[phone clatters]
ALYI: That is the company telling us.

53
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:14,338
NELEH: Then we'll write
step four ourselves.

54
00:03:14,422 --> 00:03:18,083
[dialing; phone rings]

55
00:03:18,167 --> 00:03:22,292
Mario, it's Neleh, from the NopeAI board.
I'll be direct.

56
00:03:22,375 --> 00:03:27,083
The board is offering you the job of CEO,
and it wants to discuss a merger.

57
00:03:27,167 --> 00:03:28,750
MARIO: Neleh, hi. Wow.

58
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:31,417
I've actually written up some
thoughts on exactly this.

59
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:34,375
Eleven pages, on the conditions under
which we might, hypothetically—

60
00:03:34,458 --> 00:03:36,542
ADELINA: In plain English: no.

61
00:03:36,625 --> 00:03:37,917
[dial tone; phone rings]

62
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,958
It's Nozama. About the money.

63
00:03:40,042 --> 00:03:42,708
MARIO: Hi. Yes. We're very worried.
How much?

64
00:03:46,667 --> 00:03:48,750
NELEH: He's been in
the building for hours.

65
00:03:48,833 --> 00:03:52,625
We've talked all day about him
coming back, and we're no closer.

66
00:03:52,792 --> 00:03:55,167
ALYI: They gave him a guest badge.

67
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:58,309
NELEH: It's the correct badge.
He doesn't work here.

68
00:04:03,667 --> 00:04:06,417
Ttemme, we'd like you
to serve as interim CEO.

69
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:08,667
You already have an interim CEO.

70
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:10,458
We'd like a different one.

71
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:14,792
Fine. But before I say yes,
I need to know why you fired him.

72
00:04:17,250 --> 00:04:18,375
Okay.

73
00:04:19,125 --> 00:04:21,042
Chat… for how long?

74
00:04:24,792 --> 00:04:26,958
[keys jingle]

75
00:04:27,042 --> 00:04:29,917
Good evening.
You'll want to hear our statement.

76
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,500
We look forward to getting to know Ttemme

77
00:04:31,583 --> 00:04:34,667
and NopeAI's new leadership
team and working with them.

78
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:38,667
And we're extremely excited to share the
news that Mas Manalt and Gerg Mockbran,

79
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:41,458
together with colleagues,
will be joining Macrosoft

80
00:04:41,542 --> 00:04:44,458
to lead a new advanced AI research team.

81
00:04:48,292 --> 00:04:49,583
NELEH: Step four?

82
00:05:01,625 --> 00:05:03,583
The badge was a joke.

83
00:05:04,125 --> 00:05:05,375
Mostly.

84
00:05:05,917 --> 00:05:07,208
[call rings]

85
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:09,833
GERG: Sorry, one sec.
I've got a build compiling.

86
00:05:09,917 --> 00:05:11,667
MAS: It's two in the morning, Gerg.

87
00:05:11,750 --> 00:05:14,958
GERG: Best time there is.
Nobody else is pushing anything.

88
00:05:15,042 --> 00:05:18,708
Anyway, that's not why I called.
You've got the staff letter open?

89
00:05:18,792 --> 00:05:20,125
Scroll down.

90
00:05:20,875 --> 00:05:23,792
They're telling the board they're
“…unable to work for or with people

91
00:05:23,875 --> 00:05:28,042
that lack competence, judgement and
care for our mission and employees.”

92
00:05:28,125 --> 00:05:31,208
And they'll quit, “…unless all
current board members resign…”

93
00:05:31,292 --> 00:05:32,917
MAS: And go to Macrosoft.

94
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:37,292
GERG: Yep. Macrosoft's promised them
“…positions for all NopeAI employees…”

95
00:05:37,375 --> 00:05:39,042
MAS: That's a lot of desks.

96
00:05:39,125 --> 00:05:40,713
GERG: Scroll to the bottom.

97
00:05:41,625 --> 00:05:42,875
Alyi signed it.

98
00:05:43,292 --> 00:05:44,667
MAS: Alyi voted.

99
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:46,000
GERG: He did both.

100
00:05:46,083 --> 00:05:47,625
[slot whirs]

101
00:05:47,667 --> 00:05:51,431
That'll be the share sale.
Everybody's been waiting on that one.

102
00:05:51,515 --> 00:05:52,708
[stamp thuds]

103
00:05:52,792 --> 00:05:54,333
MAS: What are you building?

104
00:05:54,417 --> 00:05:57,083
GERG: The company. Again. Just in case.

105
00:05:58,333 --> 00:06:00,667
So. Do I tell everyone to pack?

106
00:06:01,125 --> 00:06:03,167
MAS: Ask me when it compiles.

107
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:05,625
[a key turns in a lock]

108
00:06:05,625 --> 00:06:09,792
TASYA: Don't get up, Mas.
I won't keep you. Everyone is welcome.

109
00:06:10,042 --> 00:06:11,208
MAS: Everyone.

110
00:06:11,292 --> 00:06:15,167
TASYA: Yes. You first.
And there's a desk for every one of them.

111
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,292
MAS: Leave it open.

112
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:24,000
[swing band music]

113
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:28,132
NELEH: Has anyone read the char—

114
00:06:32,208 --> 00:06:34,500
[music stops]

115
00:06:41,875 --> 00:06:43,667
You sent three.

116
00:06:43,833 --> 00:06:45,583
One for each day.

117
00:06:45,875 --> 00:06:48,167
It has been four days.

118
00:06:48,250 --> 00:06:50,208
I'm not counting today.

119
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,208
MAS: What happens to you
if NopeAI disappears?

120
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:58,875
TASYA: Oh, we'd be fine.

121
00:06:58,958 --> 00:07:01,958
…we have all the IP rights
and all the capability…

122
00:07:02,042 --> 00:07:05,292
We are below them,
above them, around them.

123
00:07:06,708 --> 00:07:08,473
TASYA (from the floor): Hello.

124
00:07:08,556 --> 00:07:10,375
[fire crackles]

125
00:07:10,417 --> 00:07:13,500
[door bangs open]

126
00:07:13,625 --> 00:07:15,750
Which room is on fire?

127
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:17,958
…Ah.

128
00:07:18,833 --> 00:07:22,333
Before this goes out, I'm reading
it once, so nobody's surprised.

129
00:07:22,417 --> 00:07:25,875
We have reached an agreement in principle
for Mas Manalt to return to NopeAI

130
00:07:25,958 --> 00:07:30,917
as CEO with a new initial board of Terb
(Chair), the Other Yrral, and Mada.

131
00:07:31,292 --> 00:07:32,708
You're staying?

132
00:07:33,083 --> 00:07:36,250
He stays.
You and Gerg don't sit on the board.

133
00:07:36,333 --> 00:07:37,542
We'll stand.

134
00:07:37,625 --> 00:07:40,292
And there'll be an independent review.

135
00:07:40,375 --> 00:07:41,625
Of what?

136
00:07:41,708 --> 00:07:42,625
[music stops]

137
00:07:42,708 --> 00:07:44,125
MADA: Good question.

138
00:07:44,542 --> 00:07:46,000
MAS: Good question.

139
00:07:57,667 --> 00:07:59,500
TTEMME: Chat, we're so back.

140
00:07:59,583 --> 00:08:02,833
[glass shatters; neon buzzes on]

141
00:08:05,875 --> 00:08:07,500
[error tone]

142
00:08:08,958 --> 00:08:10,208
MAS: Okay.

143
00:08:10,792 --> 00:08:14,208
[low hum]

144
00:08:14,375 --> 00:08:15,417
Is it ready?

145
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:17,000
It's a preview.

146
00:08:17,083 --> 00:08:19,025
You said that about the last one.

147
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,125
MAS: I love and respect Alyi,

148
00:08:27,208 --> 00:08:31,833
I think he's a guiding light of the
field and a gem of a human being.

149
00:08:31,917 --> 00:08:34,875
I harbor zero ill will towards him.

